  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of agro-ecology for sustainable agriculture for farmers&#x2019; resilience building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a pilot project seeking to explore the opportunities for agroecological approaches to contribute to resilient livelihoods and ecological sustainability in Sierra Leone. The country is at a crossroads facing multiple vulnerabilities of climate change impact, food insecurity, weak governance, and poor economic performance. These conditions are driving the already poor population into deeper poverty, with deepening food insecurity. The country is in a critical situation, facing severe hunger.
Because agro-ecology practices are limited and not consciously practiced in Sierra Leone, its practices will improve ecological conditions, this project is an opportunity to explore its potential in the country, and capture learning and evidence to take forward further agroecological support to farmers as well as policy advocacy and behavioral change advocacy actions related to agro-ecology and food systems. The agroecology support activities of the project will take place in 9 villages in Kpaka chiefdom, Pujehun district and will target a total of 270 direct farmer beneficiaries. Farmers will be identified and organized into groups. They will be empowered through training on agroecology and its principles and practices in theory and utilizing the Farmer Fields School approach in demonstrating what will be taught in the theory training. Farmers will be supported through ongoing accompaniment and practical/financial support to implement contextually appropriate agro-ecological techniques on their farms. Working with local farmers and technical experts in agro-ecology, the project will also gather learning and evidence about the best way forward for promoting agro-ecology in Sierra Leone.  The intervention will further engage in research or studies to generate data for the understanding of agroecology in Sierra Leone, while at the same time using that data for the purpose of advocacy and setting solutions to policy level challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
